{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to","id":440248,"title":"Changing Breeds 2.0- Because Someone had to","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T12:00:07-07:00","id":440248,"title":"Changing Breeds 2.0- Because Someone had to","content":"I'm writing a homebrew conversion of Changing Breeds to bring them in line with W:tF 2.0. Most of the work has been easy so far, coming up with unified Breeds that balance with Uratha, but the difficult part is dealing with unique special powers for Dire Beast and Primal Beast, as the ones Urshul and Urhan get aren't perfect for every breed. Leaning on converting the subspecies into Tribes, as far as Gifts, Renown, and the Hunt are concerned, while moving away from Aspects &amp; Favors toward having Breed Gifts, much like the Gifts of the Wolf.<br /> <br /> I'll post my notes in a bit, but I'm open to suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:15:11-07:00","id":440278,"title":"","content":"Changing Breeds gets a lot of flak for a lot of good reasons, but I've always liked playing around with them. When I first started my Werewolf game, my &quot;pack&quot; included four different breeds (plus a Siten Uzu which had been adapted for ravens). I had to give the mechanics a critical eye, and completely invented my own lore and fluff for them, but having them as an option can add interesting depth to the setting. So, I totally appreciate someone working on a 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:22:36-07:00","id":440286,"title":"","content":"You can look in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\">here </a>for an early attempt and previous suggestions for both fluff and mechanics fixes. I personally suggested the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/326192-setting-material-the-old-ones\">Old Ones</a> as a potential antagonistic force, and I do plan on developing them in a way that would make them quite different then the idigams. If you want any help, I'm here :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:28:31-07:00","id":440292,"title":"","content":"This should get moved to WoD general discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:38:09-07:00","id":440307,"title":"","content":"I really hope OP decides to do a 2ed of changing breeds. I'm working on an ancient era for werewolf and I'm trying to convert the Balam to 2ed rules &amp; mechanics. Though I am not sure how the gifts will work out....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:50:15-07:00","id":440346,"title":"","content":"Changing Breeds really needs to be update and totally reimagened to 2e. Maybe integrating other elements like the shapshifters from War Against the Pure and Skinchangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:55:04-07:00","id":440439,"title":"","content":"If they could do away with rape implications in the introductory chapter, that'd be awesome too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:58:13-07:00","id":440505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=440286#post440286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can look in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/33067-ancients-awaken-the-old-ones-chronicles-changing-breeds-discussion-brainstorming\">here </a>for an early attempt and previous suggestions for both fluff and mechanics fixes. I personally suggested the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/326192-setting-material-the-old-ones\">Old Ones</a> as a potential antagonistic force, and I do plan on developing them in a way that would make them quite different then the idigams. If you want any help, I'm here :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the &quot;lost tribe&quot; angle for the Old Ones. An entire Cryptopoly of Shadow-bound Shifters, using Reaching and Gifts to manipulate a world they're forevermore denied? I think that has potential.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:11:29-07:00","id":440517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=440278#post440278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing Breeds gets a lot of flak for a lot of good reasons, but I've always liked playing around with them. When I first started my Werewolf game, my &quot;pack&quot; included four different breeds (plus a Siten Uzu which had been adapted for ravens). I had to give the mechanics a critical eye, and completely invented my own lore and fluff for them, but having them as an option can add interesting depth to the setting. So, I totally appreciate someone working on a 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>If CB was to get another shot, I would put them in the same class as the Uratha.<br /> <br /> What do the Uratha do? They hunt. The Wolf Must Hunt. It's what wolves do and it's what the Uratha do.<br /> <br /> What do Ravens do? They steal.<br /> <br /> What do Sharks do? They swim.<br /> <br /> etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Link a spirit patron (Luna and Father Wolf shouldn't be the only one squirting out kids) and combine it with a role in the Shadow<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:56:10-07:00","id":440641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=440517#post440517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If CB was to get another shot, I would put them in the same class as the Uratha.<br /> <br /> What do the Uratha do? They hunt. The Wolf Must Hunt. It's what wolves do and it's what the Uratha do.<br /> <br /> What do Ravens do? They steal.<br /> <br /> What do Sharks do? They swim.<br /> <br /> etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Link a spirit patron (Luna and Father Wolf shouldn't be the only one squirting out kids) and combine it with a role in the Shadow<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's brilliantly simple. Thanks Shock, you just solved one of my big road blocks in how to bring other shifters into my upcoming chronicle!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:34:02-07:00","id":440665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=440439#post440439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they could do away with rape implications in the introductory chapter, that'd be awesome too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dear I had tried to forget that part. I hate to say it but CB was a really shitty book. A lot of the stuff in it was broken.<br /> Skinchangers on the other hand.. That one still is in my top 10 if not top 5 of 1E NWoD.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T19:12:19-07:00","id":440780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=440641#post440641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's brilliantly simple. Thanks Shock, you just solved one of my big road blocks in how to bring other shifters into my upcoming chronicle!</div> </div> </div> </div>If you really want to subvert views that the Uratha/players have, start to drop hints that those who are taken over by Rat/Spider Hosts are not outright killed but merge with them and act in the same Uratha do. Azlu Crawlers are less &quot;Evil spider who crawls into people's ears to munch on their brains&quot; and more &quot;Spirit shard which is piloted by a gestalt compound of souls that it has consumed and continues to act according to it's instincts&quot; Not much different from a Kindred who has committed Diablerie. Glimmers of specks of humanity screaming as it is forced to enact more and more destruction by hard wired predatory urges. <br /> <br /> Azarath, simply enough, don't lose their souls as Uratha claim they do. The Azlu shard merges with said human in which full body horror with psychological torment comes into play.<br /> <br /> Same thing with the Rats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T20:09:15-07:00","id":440815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=440517#post440517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If CB was to get another shot, I would put them in the same class as the Uratha.<br /> <br /> What do the Uratha do? They hunt. The Wolf Must Hunt. It's what wolves do and it's what the Uratha do.<br /> <br /> What do Ravens do? They steal.<br /> <br /> What do Sharks do? They swim.<br /> <br /> etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Link a spirit patron (Luna and Father Wolf shouldn't be the only one squirting out kids) and combine it with a role in the Shadow<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I'd go too. I did want to use the Sacred Hunt to describe where Uratha and other Shifters would interact (and coming up with a way to avoid the Uratha killing off other Shifters out of hand, Pure/Bale Hound, and to a lesser extent, BT shenanigans aside), but it would work better if I could take into account the metaphysics of why those power animals are revered, and giving them their own Breed Gifts is a step in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T20:33:28-07:00","id":440824,"title":"","content":"Here is what I've done so far from the <u>Changing Breeds</u> book. As I said before, the issue I have is dealing with how Dire Beast and Primal Beast forms aren't all going to do the same things Urshul and Urhan do.<br /> <br /> <b>Breed:</b> Bastet<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -