book? How &quot;Breed&quot; encompasses several &quot;Species&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not the way biology works, and even if this is a magical world of magic and magic, <i>sheeeeeeesh</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T10:55:38-07:00","id":444543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=444058#post444058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know one of the things that bothered me most consistently about the CB book? How &quot;Breed&quot; encompasses several &quot;Species&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not the way biology works, and even if this is a magical world of magic and magic, <i>sheeeeeeesh</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Platonic Metaphysics, and design limits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:14:17-07:00","id":444570,"title":"","content":"They're all different breeds of <i>human</i>. Sort of. <br /> <br /> Speaking of, 2e shapeshifters might be able to breed with each other. How exactly do we handle a half-werewolf-half-weredolphin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:36:21-07:00","id":444629,"title":"","content":"In short I love this, it will save alot of trouble for me when making my own game.<br /> <br /> In regards to shifters breeding I'd say that if they are both equal then I'll roll a die to see what race the child gets, or if one side can be argued to be &quot;stronger&quot; like higher &quot;Primal Urge&quot;, a more shifters in the near lineage etc. than the child will belong to that race. That's how I'll do it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:39:30-07:00","id":444633,"title":"","content":"One way that always irked me about changing breed was how insanely powerful as good as everything in there was compared to an uratha. IF you had the right powers from the book you could do almost everything an uratha could do and were better at that thanks to way higher stats (given with the background that they should hunt almost everything it was almost a joke how weak even a pack of them was compared to some of the changers in the book). <br /> <br /> Thus the question is are the uratha the limit or are the others as strong / stronger (one should not forget that some of these species like lions also tend to move around in packs as wolves do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:53:41-07:00","id":444647,"title":"","content":"WATP had each form limited to getting the same number of bonus dots as it's werewolf equivalent. That seems like a good limit to impose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:40:30-07:00","id":445015,"title":"","content":"My main problem with Changing Breeds was the assumption that almost every type of animal had a shapeshifting breed. I like my shapeshifters to be somewhat rare, for example Werewolves and maybe a few other types that are preferably more than reskinned Werewolves for other animal types. So the idea of Changing Breeds as some sort of canon does not appeal to me, but I'll grant that it has some toolbox uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:44:40-07:00","id":445018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440248-changing-breeds-2-0-because-someone-had-to?p=444633#post444633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way that always irked me about changing breed was how insanely powerful as good as everything in there was compared to an uratha. IF you had the right powers from the book you could do almost everything an uratha could do and were better at that thanks to way higher stats (given with the background that they should hunt almost everything it was almost a joke how weak even a pack of them was compared to some of the changers in the book).<br /> <br /> Thus the question is are the uratha the limit or are the others as strong / stronger (one should not forget that some of these species like lions also tend to move around in packs as wolves do).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I'm hard-coding form abilities and having everyone use Gifts and Auspices, to avoid as much of that as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/membe